# ---------------- Enemy_Walls.events (Task 7 Part G2: a chase that rounds corners) ----------------
# The Part G1 line-of-sight chase with one opt-in qualifier:
#
#     move toward player speed 60 around walls
#
# While that chase runs, the C# bridge corner-samples: the straight probe toward the player is
# tested first, and only when it is blocked (or the enemy is stuck) does a short ray fan or the
# wall tangent pick a heading around the obstacle. Patrol still uses `goto` (NavMesh), so this
# variant needs no baked NavMesh for the chase itself — but the walls DO need colliders, the
# same requirement `me sees` already has.
#
# Difference from Enemy_LOS.events: losing the sight ray behind a corner no longer flips
# straight to `hunt`. The sheet keeps chasing for 1.5 s while the steering rounds the corner;
# `sees player` cancels the hand-off by switching the mode back to "chase". Only when there is
# really no way round does it fall into G1's blind `hunt` arc, then back to patrol.
#
# Isolation: Enemy_LOS.events and TK4Controls.scene are untouched. Attach this sheet to a
# second enemy (an explicit EventSheet component, or an actor named Enemy_Walls) to compare.

when me appears
  enemy type "Zombie"
  set my mode to "patrol"
  print "Enemy_Walls: patrol start"
  goto random Waypoint speed 100 facing forward

when me arrives at Waypoint
  my mode is "patrol"                        # don't hijack a hunt or chase
  my Speed is higher than 0
  wait random 0.5 to 2 seconds
  goto random Waypoint speed 100 facing forward

when me sees player by my SightDistance
  set my mode to "chase"
  stop moving                                # cancel the patrol goto — the chase is direct
  print "Enemy_Walls: chase start"

# ---- sight broke: round the corner first, hunt only if there is no way through ----
when me stops seeing player
  my mode is "chase"
  set my mode to "round"
  print "Enemy_Walls: sight broke, rounding the corner"
  wait 1.5 seconds
  my mode is "round"                         # still round (never reacquired)? hand over to hunt
  set my mode to "hunt"
  print "Enemy_Walls: no way round, hunting"
  wait 6 seconds
  my mode is "hunt"                          # still hunting? back to patrol
  set my mode to "patrol"
  print "Enemy_Walls: hunt gave up, back to patrol"
  goto random Waypoint speed 100 facing forward

# G1's blind arc: not pathfinding, a sweep that reacquires the moment a ray clears.
when every 0.5 seconds
  my mode is "hunt"
  turn left degrees 45
  move forward speed 40

# Chase AND round steer with the wall-aware move; patrol and hunt leave it alone.
when every 0.02 seconds
  my mode is not "patrol"
  my mode is not "hunt"
  my Speed is higher than 0                  # a rooted type stays still
  move toward player speed 60 around walls facing forward

when me is near player by 1.5
  my mode is "chase"
  my Hostile is true
  send message "hurt" to nearest player
